# What the source distribution carries beyond the package itself. README and
# LICENSE arrive on their own, named by `readme` and `license-files`; the
# changelog needs this line. All three are this tool's own files rather than
# links into the repository root — see the note in `pyproject.toml`.
#
# `examples/` is deliberately absent. `hmd lint --root examples/small` working
# straight out of an unpacked archive is the one property that would buy, and the
# fixture is a repository fixture that both implementations lint: it lives at the
# root, one copy, and a reader who wants to run it clones the repository, which
# is what the README tells them to do.
#
# The test suite is deliberately absent for a related reason. `tools/hmd/tests`
# would now travel cleanly — the repository-wide guards that could not,
# `test_docs.py` and `test_mkdocs.py`, live at the repository root and are not
# part of this project — but gates are run from a checkout, not from an sdist,
# and shipping a suite invites someone to run it as if it were one.
include CHANGELOG.md
